  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppS&E 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A pharmaceutical company is required to collect long-term safety data
    on a newly approved cancer treatment and submit regular safety updates to regulators.


    <b>Which
    authority is responsible for carrying out this ongoing monitoring and reporting?</b>'
  explanation: After approval, the study sponsor is responsible for collecting safety
    data and submitting required reports to regulatory agencies. They help track
    how the treatment performs in real-world use and make sure any new safety information
    is shared, reviewed, and addressed over time.
  correctAnswer: Study sponsor
  incorrectAnswer1: Scientific Review Committee (SRC)
  incorrectAnswer2: Data and Safety Monitoring Board (DSMB)
  incorrectAnswer3: Institutional Review Board (IRB)
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
